# openOODA v2: Comprehensive Zero-Trust Capability Model

**Location:** `openOODA/CAPS.oot`  
**Scope:** V2 capability catalog for product and `std/src/ooda/`  
**Purpose:** Single list agents must read when gating code. Mirrors `DESIGN.oot` §3.1 + V2 Architecture. Status lives in `PM.oot` §3.

**In plain English:** Before, one network token gave full access. Now we split it into small tokens. You give only what the code needs from `main()`. Each token is checked when you compile. At run time the process re-checks a process-local seal before the effect runs; forged or missing tokens fail closed. **[STATUS: path-A process-local token re-check. CAP-G1 net + CAP-G2 fs preferred maps path-A. CAP-G3 unused grants FIXED residual-only: Process/Sync/Mem/HW/UI/Sign = type accept + grant + exact require stubs; **no sealed product ops** (do not invent CameraCap product). Emit type-driven main-param inject residual (DE1). **CAP-G4 FIXED** ProcessCap preferred for exec/spawn. **CAP-G5 FIXED residual:** no product seccomp-bpf (dead stub removed). **CAP-G6 FIXED net+fs product facade wave** + **ProcessCap product facades FIXED** (2026-08-12): `process_spawn`/`wait`/`kill`/`exec` take `&ProcessCap`; `async` spawn takes ProcessCap, join stays SysCap; **python stays SysCap** (hard residual — do not migrate). Smoke: `cap_g6_std_migrate_smoke.sh` + `cap_process_facade_smoke.sh` + `cap_g4_process_smoke.sh`. Rollup: `audit/cap_process_facade_rollup.oot`. **Honesty: SysCap bulk residual** (~571 hits under `std/src`; domain stubs + hard Sys ops) — full SysCap purge **not** claimed. Unforgeable object-caps residual — do **not** claim full OS isolation. 8-byte token randomness residual; see DESIGN §3.1]**

The core principle is **least privilege at the compiler**. Every capability is checked at compile time and enforced at run time.

Here is the master list of `&Cap` tokens in the V2 ecosystem. **Count note:** `DESIGN.oot` §V2 Architecture counts **18** new granular tokens that fractured `SysCap`/`NetCap`. The list below shows **28** entries because it keeps the 2 legacy broad tokens for compat plus 8 related tokens (`EnvCap`, `MemCap`, `FfiCap`, `CryptoCap`, etc.) that DESIGN groups under §3. **`is_cap_type` accepts all 28.** Use granular tokens for **new** `std/` and product code. **Type accept ≠ sealed product path.**

### Path-A honesty (do not greenwash)

| Layer | What is true today |
|-------|--------------------|
| **Type accept** | All 28 names below are valid `&Cap` types in check (`oodac/check_cap_util.oo`). |
| **Sealed ops (net / CAP-G1)** | **path-A:** `sealed_net_kind_of` returns preferred Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind/NetCap; check accepts exact preferred **or** legacy NetCap; wrong granular denied (HttpCap↛`tcp_bind`). Smoke: `cap_g1_net_granular_smoke.sh`. |
| **Sealed ops (fs / CAP-G2)** | **path-A:** `sealed_fs_kind_of` returns preferred FsReadCap/FsWriteCap; check accepts exact preferred **or** legacy FsCap supersede; wrong granular denied (FsWriteCap↛`read_file`; FsReadCap↛`write_file`). Helpers: `cap_fs_granted_ok` / `cap_fs_argflow_ok`. |
| **Sealed ops (sys / CAP-G4)** | **FIXED path-A:** `sys_exec`/`sys_spawn`/`sys_wait`/`sys_kill` prefer **ProcessCap**; SysCap supersede. Hard **SysCap only:** `python_embed`, `async_join`, `sys_epoll_create`/`sys_inotify_init`/`sys_prctl`. |
| **Sealed ops (HW / UI — CAP-G3 residual-only)** | **`UsbCap` / `AudioCap` / `CameraCap` / `HidCap` / `WindowCap` / `FrameCap`:** residual-only — type accept + grant + **exact-token** `oo_cap_require_*` stubs; **no** check sealed ops, **no** product emit lower, **no** product free-call API. Do **not** claim HW/UI product enforce. (`GpuCap` remains legacy sealed for `gpu_launch` only.) |
| **Runtime require (net)** | **path-A:** `oo_cap_require_{http,tcp,udp,bind}` accept granular **or** `g_tok_net`; `sock_raw` NetCap-only. **Not** OS seccomp isolation of sockets. |
| **Runtime require (fs)** | **path-A:** `oo_cap_require_fsread` / `oo_cap_require_fswrite` accept granular **or** `g_tok_fs` (FsCap supersede). Wrong granular fails closed. Write still gated by **`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`** policy overlay. **Not** OS path sandbox / landlock / full FS isolation. |
| **Runtime require (CAP-G3 residual)** | **path-A residual-only:** `oo_cap_require_{process,sync,mem,audio,camera,usb,hid,window,frame,sign}` = **exact** `g_tok_*` only (fail-closed forge). **No** product op lowers them. Not a CameraCap/AudioCap product claim. |
| **Runtime grants / emit inject** | Header + runtime grant many V2 names (incl. residual HW/UI/Process). **Emit today:** fixed-name main inject only — `fs`/`sys`/`env`/`net`/`time`/`rand`/`alloc`/`ffi`/`thread`/`gpu` (`c_emit_fn.oo`). Type-driven inject for every main param (**DE1**) residual for product granular paths (`FsReadCap`→`grant_fsread`, …). Residual-only CAP-G3 family needs no inject until sealed ops exist. |
| **Unused V2 grants (CAP-G3 / SPRINT 4.3)** | **FIXED residual-only honesty:** Process/Sync/Mem + HW/UI + Sign catalogued residual; require stubs exact-token only; **no** sealed product ops. Emit inject for product granular (G1/G2 main params) remains **DE1 residual** — orthogonal to unused-grant residual-only close. |
| **Policy overlays (not Cap types)** | `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` on writes; `sys_exec` child env filter (`OODA_`/`OO_` + minimal PATH); FFI nested-`dlopen` refuse — see residual links. |
| **Not a Cap** | `// SECRET:` taint / sink refuse is **IFC**, not a capability token. Do not add SECRET to this list. |
| **Isolation ceiling** | Process-local tokens + check refuse. **Do not claim** full OS isolation, complete `seccomp-bpf`/`SIGSYS` coverage, or unforgeable object-caps across hostile rewrite. |
| **Std migration (CAP-G6)** | **FIXED path-A for net+fs product facade wave** (2026-08-12). Product: `ooda/std/os/fs.oo` → FsRead/FsWrite; `ooda/std/os/net.oo` → Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind (`sock_raw` NetCap-only). External: `std/src/fs.oo` + `std/src/net.oo` twins + domain honesty (wireguard UdpCap residual, mTLS TcpCap, select cps/ai). Smoke: `scripts/cap_g6_std_migrate_smoke.sh` exit 0. **ProcessCap product facades FIXED** residual same day: `ooda/std/os/process.oo` spawn/wait/kill/exec → `&ProcessCap` (epoll/inotify/prctl stay SysCap); `async.oo` spawn → ProcessCap, join → SysCap; external `std/async.oo` twin. **Honesty — python stays SysCap** (`python.oo` / `python_embed` hard Sys only — not ProcessCap). Smoke: `cap_process_facade_smoke.sh`. **DNS residual FIXED (UdpCap preferred):** `ooda/std/src/net/dns.oo` `resolve_ipv4` takes **`&UdpCap`** (was SOFT_LEGACY NetCap). Smoke: `cap_dns_udp_smoke.sh` exit 0. Close: `audit/cap_dns_udp_rollup.oot`. **Honesty — still no real UDP DNS product** (localhost hardcode + Err residual) — cap preferred ≠ resolver product. **batch_2 phantom honesty:** prior `audit/std_caps_batch_2.oot` claimed `http_server` / `dns_server` / `mqtt` / `websocket` / `quic` migrated under `std/src/net/` — those five paths **do not exist** on disk (live net domain = `wireguard.oo` + product facades + `ooda/std/src/net/dns.oo`). Do **not** cite batch_2 five as CAP-G6 land evidence. **Not claimed:** full std SysCap/NetCap/FsCap purge. **SysCap bulk residual** (~571 lines under `std/src`; inventory `audit/cap_g6_syscap_inventory.oot`). Evidence: `audit/cap_g6_phalanx_rollup.oot` + `audit/cap_process_facade_rollup.oot` + `audit/cap_dns_udp_rollup.oot` + peers. |

### CAP-G1 path-A map (net)

**Legacy supersede:** `&NetCap` may satisfy soft-granular preferred ops (one-wave compat). **Hard NetCap-only:** `sock_raw` / `raw_socket`.

| Preferred cap | Sealed ops (product or residual emit) | Runtime require (target) |
|---------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| **`&HttpCap`** | `fetch`; residual names `http_get` / `net_get` / `net_connect` / `downloadData` / `query_remote_api` | `oo_cap_require_http` (or NetCap) |
| **`&TcpCap`** | `tcp_connect` / `tcp_write` / `tcp_read` / `tcp_close` / `tls_connect` | `oo_cap_require_tcp` (or NetCap) |
| **`&BindCap`** | `tcp_bind` | `oo_cap_require_bind` (or NetCap) |
| **`&UdpCap`** | `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` | `oo_cap_require_udp` (or NetCap) |
| **`&NetCap`** (only) | `sock_raw` / `raw_socket` | `oo_cap_require_net` — always Err residual product |

**New code:** prefer the granular token that matches the op. **CAP-G6 path-A product facades:** `ooda/std/os/net.oo` + `std/src/net.oo` `http_get`/`net_get` → `&HttpCap`; tcp/udp/bind facades → Tcp/Udp/Bind; `sock_raw` stays NetCap. **Compat:** `&NetCap` still supersedes soft-granular at check+runtime for residual call sites.

### CAP-G2 path-A map (fs)

**Legacy supersede:** `&FsCap` may satisfy soft-granular preferred fs ops (one-wave compat). **No hard FsCap-only product op** (unlike net `sock_raw`); broad `FsCap` is supersede-only for soft read/write. **Wrong granular fail-closed:** `FsReadCap` must **not** authorize write; `FsWriteCap` must **not** authorize read/path/size.

| Preferred cap | Sealed ops (product or residual emit) | Runtime require (target) |
|---------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| **`&FsReadCap`** | `read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size` | `oo_cap_require_fsread` (or FsCap) |
| **`&FsWriteCap`** | `write_file` / `fs_write` | `oo_cap_require_fswrite` (or FsCap) + **`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`** overlay |

**New code:** prefer `&FsReadCap` for read/probe/size, `&FsWriteCap` for create/modify. **CAP-G6 path-A product facades:** `ooda/std/os/fs.oo` + `std/src/fs.oo` use FsRead/FsWrite (not legacy FsCap on signatures). **Compat:** `&FsCap` still supersedes soft-granular for residual call sites. **Not claimed:** OS FS isolation, landlock, or complete `seccomp-bpf` on open/write (CAP-G5 residual honesty).

### 1. File System & Memory
* **`&FsCap`**: Broad filesystem access **(legacy — supersedes soft-granular FsReadCap/FsWriteCap for one-wave compat). Prefer granular below for new APIs.**
* **`&FsReadCap`**: Preferred for read/probe sealed ops (`read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size`). **Must not** authorize write alone (CAP-G2 path-A). Emit type→`grant_fsread` residual (**DE1**).
* **`&FsWriteCap`**: Preferred for create/modify sealed ops (`write_file` / `fs_write`). **Must not** authorize read/path/size alone. Writes still fail-closed under `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` (policy overlay, not a Cap type). Emit type→`grant_fswrite` residual (**DE1**).
* **`&AllocCap`**: Permission to allocate heap memory (`malloc`/`free`). Product sealed + emit inject path-A.
* **`&MemCap`**: Shared memory / `mmap` across boundaries. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** type accept + `oo_cap_grant_mem` + exact `oo_cap_require_mem` stub; **no** sealed ops / product lower.

### 2. Network & Web
* **`&NetCap`**: Broad network access **(legacy — supersedes soft-granular Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind for one-wave compat; required for `sock_raw` / `raw_socket`). Prefer granular below for new APIs.**
* **`&HttpCap`**: Preferred for HTTP-ish sealed ops (`fetch` product; other names residual emit). **Must not** authorize raw bind/connect alone. Emit type→`grant_http` residual (**DE1**).
* **`&TcpCap`**: Preferred for client TCP slot IO + `tls_connect` (TLS product only when OpenSSL linked). Emit type→`grant_tcp` residual (**DE1**).
* **`&UdpCap`**: Preferred for UDP bind/recv **and** DNS residual (`ooda/std/src/net/dns.oo` `resolve_ipv4` — UDP query path; real socket DNS still residual Err). Emit type→`grant_udp` residual (**DE1**). **Not** a claim that product DNS is implemented.
* **`&BindCap`**: Preferred for TCP listen/bind (`tcp_bind`). Emit type→`grant_bind` residual (**DE1**).

### 3. OS & Execution
* **`&SysCap`**: Broad OS execution **(legacy — prefer ProcessCap for spawn/exec where CAP-G4 applies; kept for compat + hard Sys residual).** **CAP-G6 honesty:** bulk domain `std/src` still threads `&SysCap` (~571 line hits / inventory) — residual, not migrated. **Product hard-Sys facades that stay SysCap:** `python.oo` (`python_embed`), `process_*` epoll/inotify/prctl, `async` join.
* **`&ProcessCap`**: Spawn/exec/wait/kill (**CAP-G4 path-A preferred** for `sys_exec` et al.). Legacy `&SysCap` still supersedes. Does **not** unlock hard Sys residual (`sys_prctl`, `python_embed`, epoll/inotify, `async_join`). **Product facades FIXED:** `std/os/process.oo` spawn/wait/kill/exec take `&ProcessCap`; `async` `spawn_task` takes ProcessCap; smoke `cap_process_facade_smoke.sh`. **Not claimed:** domain std mass-migrate off SysCap.
* **`&SyncCap`**: IPC / Mutexes / Semaphores only. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** type accept + grant + exact `oo_cap_require_sync` stub; mutex product path remains `&ThreadCap`.
* **`&ThreadCap`**: Spawn parallel CPU threads. Product sealed (mutex/spawn/join/channel).
* **`&EnvCap`**: Read environment variables. Product sealed.

### 4. Hardware & Peripherals
* **`&GpuCap`**: Run parallel work on the GPU/NPU. Product sealed for `gpu_launch` only (noop/cpu path-A; device shaders residual).
* **`&UsbCap`**: Direct hardware passthrough (for I2C). **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops.
* **`&AudioCap`**: Read mic / write speakers. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops.
* **`&CameraCap`**: Read raw video frames from a webcam. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops. Do **not** invent CameraCap product free names.
* **`&HidCap`**: Read keyboard/mouse events (checks keyloggers). **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops.

### 5. UI & Display
* **`&WindowCap`**: Request a GUI window from the OS compositor. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops.
* **`&FrameCap`**: Map pixels directly to the framebuffer (for hologram engines). **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact require stub; **no** sealed product ops.

### 6. Audit & Security
* **`&AuditCap`**: Write to the append-only, cryptographic audit trail. Residual (type accept; grant/require bodies residual vs link checklist).
* **`&SignCap`**: Use the host Secure Enclave (TPM/HSM) to sign payloads. **Residual-only (CAP-G3):** grant + exact `oo_cap_require_sign` stub; **no** sealed op matrix.
* **`&CryptoCap`**: Enforces cryptographic operations. Required for `oo_cg_sign` and `oo_cg_verify`.
* **`&HitlCap`** (Human-In-The-Loop): Residual as Cap type; product HITL path-A is `verify_human` under Env+Fs (not HitlCap seal).
* **`&TimeCap`**: Read the system clock. Without it, you cannot measure time (helps limit timing side channels). Product sealed.
* **`&RandCap`**: Read from `/dev/urandom` (cryptographically secure random). Product sealed.
* **`&FfiCap`** (`&UnsafeFFICap` alias): Run unsafe C bindings. Most dangerous. Requires explicit grant. Product sealed.

